#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Ripple control receiver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"With a **ripple control receiver** (RCR), the grid operator can remotely "
"limit the feed-in of a PV system, e.g. in the event of grid overload. The "
"usual levels are **0 %, 30 % and 60 %** of the system power (as well as 100 "
"% = no limitation). For this purpose, the receiver switches contacts that "
"are evaluated by the energy management system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The ripple control receiver is not the same as xref:user/storage-control/"
"section-14a-enwg.adoc[§ 14a control]: the RCR limits **feed-in**, § 14a "
"limits **grid purchase** (for the storage: the charging power)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two variants"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-two-variants
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS has two ways of integrating a ripple control receiver:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variant\n"
"| Connection\n"
"| Who limits\n"
"\n"
"| **Ripple control receiver** (“external limitation”)\n"
"| on the **inverter**\n"
"| the inverter itself; OpenEMS only switches on its RCR function\n"
"| **Dynamic ripple control receiver**\n"
"| on the **inputs of the control computer**\n"
"| OpenEMS: it calculates the permitted feed-in and passes it on to the inverter\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"For FENECON Home and Commercial systems, you select the variant in the "
"system app under “External limitation”: **No limitation**, **Ripple control "
"receiver** or **Dynamic ripple control receiver**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The **Home 10** (generation 1) only has a checkbox “Ripple control receiver "
"active?”; this corresponds to the first variant. The dynamic ripple control "
"receiver is not offered for the Home 10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The dynamic ripple control receiver is set up by the apps for **Home 6, Home "
"10 Gen2, Home 15, Home 20, Home 30** and for the Commercial systems 50 Gen3 "
"and 100. A prerequisite is a control computer with its own digital inputs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic ripple control receiver in detail"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-dynamic-ripple-control-receiver-in-detail
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The function is called **Controller.Ess.RippleControlReceiver** (usually "
"`+ctrlEssRippleControlReceiver0+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home-battery.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input (default)\n"
"| Level\n"
"| Permitted feed-in\n"
"\n"
"| `+…/DigitalInput2+`\n"
"| 0 %\n"
"| no feed-in\n"
"| `+…/DigitalInput3+`\n"
"| 30 %\n"
"| 30 %\n"
"| `+…/DigitalInput4+`\n"
"| 60 %\n"
"| 60 %\n"
"| no input active\n"
"| 100 %\n"
"| no limitation by the RCR\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"On these systems, the first digital input is reserved for xref:user/storage-"
"control/section-14a-enwg.adoc[§ 14a control]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"If several inputs are active at the same time, the **strictest** level "
"applies: 0 % before 30 % before 60 %."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The inputs are evaluated **inverted** (noted in the code as a peculiarity of "
"the relay board): a level is active when the input reports “off”. If an "
"input does not supply any value, it is considered inactive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid "In **island mode** there is no limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the percentages refer to"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-the-percentages-refer-to
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The percentages refer to the **maximum apparent power of the storage/hybrid "
"inverter**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"permitted feed-in = maximum inverter power × level\n"
"Example: 10 kVA inverter, level 30 %  →  maximum 3,000 W feed-in\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"If the maximum inverter power is not (yet) known, OpenEMS sets **0 W** as "
"the limit as a precaution when a level is active."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"If a general feed-in limit (e.g. 60 % rule from the system settings) applies "
"at the same time, the **smaller** of the two values is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happens to the surplus"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-to-the-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid "The permitted feed-in has an effect on two levels:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-to-the-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"**Inverter:** The limit is transferred to the inverter as a feed-in "
"limitation. It controls the PV power so that no more is fed in at the grid "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-to-the-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"**Storage:** xref:user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc[Grid-"
"optimized charge] adopts the feed-in permitted by the RCR as its limit. The "
"storage then charges the part of the PV power that may not be fed in. This "
"way, as little solar power as possible is lost through curtailment. If "
"xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[price control] is active, "
"grid-optimized charge is switched off (see next section)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-to-the-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"PV power is only actually curtailed when the storage is full or cannot "
"charge fast enough."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interaction with price control"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-interaction-with-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"If xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[price control] is "
"active, **neither planning nor ongoing control** takes the RCR level into "
"account:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-interaction-with-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"**Planning:** In the xref:user/schedule/overview.adoc[schedule], the energy "
"optimizer only calculates with the feed-in limit from the system settings or "
"the fusing of the grid connection. An RCR level could not be planned in "
"advance anyway because it cannot be foreseen."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-interaction-with-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"**Ongoing operation:** Price control protects a feed-in limit by having the "
"storage charge more (“Avoid feed-in limit”). It also only uses the limit "
"from the system settings, not the RCR level."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-interaction-with-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The limitation itself nevertheless remains effective because the inverter "
"complies with it. However, PV power may be curtailed that the storage could "
"have absorbed. This applies, for example, if the schedule currently provides "
"for delayed or limited charging because the storage is only to be charged "
"later."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-interaction-with-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"Without price control (or in “Off” mode), grid-optimized charge is at work, "
"and it takes the RCR level into account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is recorded"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Value\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| `+RestrictionMode+`\n"
"| current level: no limitation, 0 %, 30 % or 60 %\n"
"| `+CumulatedRestrictionTime+`\n"
"| total duration of all limitations in seconds (across all levels)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"Both values are stored with high priority in the xref:user/data/history-"
"rrd4j.adoc[history]. This makes it possible to trace when and for how long "
"the grid operator limited feed-in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display in the web interface"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-display-in-the-web-interface
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"In the **grid widget**, a line “Feed-in limitation” appears during a "
"limitation with the permitted feed-in in percent and a note about the ripple "
"control receiver."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-display-in-the-web-interface
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"In the **grid history**, periods with limitation are marked in the chart, as "
"are § 14a interventions and island mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-order
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The RCR controller runs in the fixed order of control functions directly "
"after the § 14a limitation and before all other storage functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variant “Ripple control receiver on the inverter”"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-variant-ripple-control-receiver-on-the-inverter
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"With this variant, the receiver is connected directly to the inverter. "
"OpenEMS only switches on the “Ripple Control Receiver” function in its "
"settings. The limitation is carried out by the inverter itself. It follows "
"that:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-variant-ripple-control-receiver-on-the-inverter
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS does **not** know the current level and does not record it."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-variant-ripple-control-receiver-on-the-inverter
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"Grid-optimized charge knows nothing about the limitation. The storage "
"therefore does not specifically charge the part that may not be fed in. The "
"inverter curtails the PV power directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-variant-ripple-control-receiver-on-the-inverter
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"For the combination with a storage system, the **dynamic** variant is "
"therefore the better choice if the system supports it."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"In OpenEMS, the percentage levels refer to the power of the **storage/hybrid "
"inverter**, not to the installed PV power (kWp). For systems whose PV power "
"differs significantly, this may differ from the specification of the grid "
"operator. If in doubt, clarify with the grid operator or installer."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The assignment of the inputs is fixed: input 2 = 0 %, input 3 = 30 %, input "
"4 = 60 %. The wiring must match."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc
msgid ""
"The RCR only limits feed-in. Self-consumption and storage charging remain "
"possible."
msgstr ""
